{
  "subtype": "focus_inference",
  "implied_focus": "The nature/type of the underlying problem in each incident ticket (categorizing recurring problem types by category, affected component, and failure symptom)",
  "per_column": [
    {
      "name": "incident_category",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Directly captures the type of problem (email, database, vpn), the core axis for identifying recurring problem types."
    },
    {
      "name": "affected_system_component",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Adds a finer-grained facet of the problem (which specific component fails), differentiating within categories."
    },
    {
      "name": "failure_symptom",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Captures the manifestation of the problem (cannot_connect, access_denied), a coherent third facet enabling problem-type clustering."
    },
    {
      "name": "recurrence_signal",
      "supports_focus": false,
      "rationale": "Constant 'true' for all 500 rows -- zero variance, no analytical value; a vacuous restatement of the query rather than a real signal."
    },
    {
      "name": "ticket_resolved",
      "supports_focus": false,
      "rationale": "Resolution status is a lifecycle/outcome attribute, not part of characterizing the problem type; peripheral to the focus."
    },
    {
      "name": "assignment_status",
      "supports_focus": false,
      "rationale": "Whether a ticket is assigned is a workflow attribute unrelated to identifying recurring problem types."
    }
  ],
  "focus_coherence": 0.72,
  "structure_quality": 0.7,
  "focus_actionability": 0.85,
  "rationale": "The first three columns (category, component, symptom) form a genuinely coherent, well-structured decomposition of 'problem type' at a useful granularity, enabling an analyst to cluster and rank recurring problem patterns -- clearly actionable. However, coherence is diluted by a grab-bag of three off-focus columns: recurrence_signal is a degenerate constant (true for all 500) adding no information, while ticket_resolved and assignment_status are workflow/lifecycle attributes rather than problem-characterizing facets. The strong core keeps the implied focus recognizable and inferable, but the extraneous columns prevent this from being a tight, single-focus structure."
}

